WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.068
-Welcome back to "Late Night"
on Thanksgiving.

00:00:02.068 --> 00:00:03.402
My family is here.

00:00:03.402 --> 00:00:06.039
But, Dad, Albert
has come in from outside.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:09.108
-Yeah. He wants to be part
of the program.

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:11.444
-That's great. Now, is that --
Is he --

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:15.415
He's in your marital bed
right now. Correct?

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:16.649
-He's in our bed.
-Yeah.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.417
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:20.786
Will he sleep
in the bed tonight?

00:00:20.786 --> 00:00:22.922
-He'll sleep in the bed
for a little while.

00:00:22.922 --> 00:00:25.325
Then he'll get on the floor.
But he will --

00:00:25.325 --> 00:00:28.762
He comes in bed
in the morning about

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.831
20, 30 minutes before it's time
to get up and gets between

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.801
the two of us
and he'll go back to sleep.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.969
And then until I roll over
and wake up

00:00:36.969 --> 00:00:42.942
and then I get this tremendous
affection to start my day.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.677
I wake up in the best mood.

00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:46.545
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.545 --> 00:00:48.314
I get a thousand kisses.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.482
I got a lot of nuzzles.

00:00:50.482 --> 00:00:53.485
-Is that a thousand when you add
up his kisses and Mom's

00:00:53.485 --> 00:00:55.388
or is that all Albert?

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.090
-It's a thousand.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:01:00.092
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:03.029
-Hey, so it's now time
for a Thanksgiving tradition

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.964
that is now seven years running,

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:08.534
which started when my firstborn,
Ashe.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:10.637
We dressed him up
as a turkey one year

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:13.106
and then we dressed
him up as a turkey again.

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:14.940
And then we dressed up him
and his brother Axel.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.543
Last year we added
our daughter Adelaide,

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:19.044
and I'm always worried the boys
are going to say,

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:21.013
"We don't want to dress up
like turkeys again.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:24.717
You know, we're not your clowns
to perform at your whim."

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:28.087
But they were very enthusiastic
about being turkeys again.

00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:32.758
So here it is, year seven of
the Meyers kids as turkeys.

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:35.995
-Happy Thanksgiving!

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.498
Da-da, happy Thanksgiving!

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:42.568
[ Audience aws ]

00:01:42.568 --> 00:01:48.274
Fly. I can fly. I can fly.
I can fly. I can fly.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:51.744
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.247 --> 00:01:57.817 line:0%
-Happy birthday.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.817 --> 00:02:01.454
-Happy Thanksgiving!

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:03.423
-Eee-goo-goo!

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:07.960
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.362
-Very nice.
-Not bad.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.998
-They did a very, very good job.

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.499
And it should be noted.

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.568
I think they all enjoy it
except for Frisbee,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.102
who hates it more
than anything in the world.

00:02:17.102 --> 00:02:18.871
-Yeah.
-It turns out most dogs

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:21.674
do not value the tradition
of Thanksgiving,

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:23.176
nor do they want
to dress like pilgrims.

00:02:23.176 --> 00:02:25.311
-And I don't think she hates it
more as it progresses.

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:27.479
I think she's always hated it
exactly as much.

00:02:27.479 --> 00:02:29.682
-She's always hated it the most
a dog could hate it.

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:30.683
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.084
-So, you know,

00:02:32.084 --> 00:02:34.621
Thanksgiving is obviously a time
to spend with family.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:37.923
But I also want to talk about
those who are no longer with us.

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:41.127
Your sister Sherry
passed away this year.

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.494
And I want to just tell

00:02:42.494 --> 00:02:45.164
a couple of my favorite stories
about Sherry,

00:02:45.164 --> 00:02:48.067
who was a wonderful aunt
and a wonderful person.

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:51.036
Now, this is a photo
when you and your sisters

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:53.305
came to the show, and there
you are sitting in a row.

00:02:53.305 --> 00:02:57.576
You might see thematically
they kind of look alike.

00:02:57.576 --> 00:02:59.044
This is Sherry there.

00:02:59.044 --> 00:03:02.481
And we refer to you
and your sisters as the geese.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:05.217
-Yes.
-Because when you are walking in

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:09.722
the street or down a hallway,
it feels like a flock of birds.

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:13.559
-Yes. And they're very loud too.
-Yes, they're very loud.

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.294
They make some noise.
But when you were here,

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:17.964
I cut to you guys.
I mentioned the geese.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:20.066
And it turned out
that resonated with some people.

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.601
-Oh, my gosh.

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:25.505
Oh, and you also made a comment
about how we were all different

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:28.574
samples of Benjamin Moore
paint, the color of our --

00:03:28.574 --> 00:03:31.377
-It looks like one paint strip
of Benjamin Moore paint.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.245
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:36.182
-So, I had gotten them tickets

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:39.318
to -- we went to see "Hamilton,"
the four of us.

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:42.054
And pretty close
to Hamilton was

00:03:42.054 --> 00:03:43.990
Don't Call --
Don't Tell Mama, a bar.

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:46.192
So we were going
to go there afterwards.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:50.896
So we're walking across
the street and a busy street,

00:03:50.896 --> 00:03:52.565
and somebody stops us and says,

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:54.567
"Wait a minute,
are you the geese?"

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.834 --> 00:04:00.239
And my sister Sherry says,
"Yes, we certainly are."

00:04:00.239 --> 00:04:04.176
So then, like another block,
the exact same thing happens.

00:04:04.176 --> 00:04:07.079
"Are you the geese?"
She was so thrilled.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:10.316
So thrilled. And then we get to
Don't Tell Mama.

00:04:10.316 --> 00:04:12.785
-Yeah, I got there early
to reserve a table.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:13.953
Don't Tell Mama is a great bar.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.155
The staff sing show tunes.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:18.991
It's very active, very lively.
It's a great time.

00:04:18.991 --> 00:04:20.927
And so, you know,
the staff is singing

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.628
and walking around
and everyone's into it.

00:04:22.628 --> 00:04:25.697
And Sherry just has her head
down on the table with a pen

00:04:25.697 --> 00:04:26.965
and cocktail napkins.

00:04:26.965 --> 00:04:28.534
And I was like, "Sherry,
what are you doing?"

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:30.435
And she's like,
"Well, we're famous now.

00:04:30.435 --> 00:04:34.173
So I'm signing napkins so I can
have something to sell."

00:04:34.173 --> 00:04:35.908
And I was like, "What are you
going to sell them for?"

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:39.211
And she thinks for a minute
and she writes $10 on one.

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:41.047
And on another one,
she's like $5.

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:42.381
I was like, "What's
the difference?"

00:04:42.381 --> 00:04:43.816
She's like,
"How bad do they want it?

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:46.085
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:48.554
-Late in life,
she had her moment of fame

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.923
and she took
great financial advantage.

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:53.826
-Yes.
-My favorite Sherry story is

00:04:53.826 --> 00:04:58.164
we went -- I took you and all
your sisters to see "Les Mis."

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:01.200
-Yes.
-And we were up in the balcony.

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.236
-Way, way up.
-Way up in the balcony.

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:05.605
-Vertiginous walk.
-Not great seats.

00:05:05.605 --> 00:05:09.642
And a vertiginous walk
is a very, very well-put

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.176
way of saying it.

00:05:11.176 --> 00:05:14.313
And Sherry was not
the most mobile of aunts.

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:16.315
-No.
-And she also --

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:19.952
Would you say she wore the most
jewelry anyone's ever worn?

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:23.322
-I would say there were
30 bracelets on each arm.

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.991
-Yeah.
-At least two rings per finger.

00:05:25.991 --> 00:05:30.096
But the bracelets
were mostly jangly bracelets.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:32.298
And my sister Alex
would take her on trips.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:34.200
And when they get
to the TSA thing,

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.467
Alex would just
throw up her hands.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:37.136
She said, "She can't
take them off.

00:05:37.136 --> 00:05:39.872
You need to get a locksmith
because they can't --"

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.173
And she couldn't.
She never took them off.

00:05:41.173 --> 00:05:43.343
She slept in them.
So it was jangle, jangle.

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:46.579
-When she walked,
I remember saying that

00:05:46.579 --> 00:05:49.148
it was like Jacob Marley
in "A Christmas Carol."

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:50.883
-Yes.
-Like, just the jangling

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:53.452
chains of a vengeful ghost.
-Yes.

00:05:53.452 --> 00:05:55.487
-And so she had
to go to the bathroom

00:05:55.487 --> 00:05:58.557
in the middle of "Les Mis,"
and I was already like --

00:05:58.557 --> 00:06:00.893
middle of the aisle,
vertiginous.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.729
She gets up, jingles down.

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:04.964
-Well, my sister Christy went
with her.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.899
-Yes.
-And she asked Christy first,

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:09.301
who always has this
huge pocketbook with her.

00:06:09.301 --> 00:06:10.903
"Do you happen to have
a flashlight in there

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:12.037
to get us to the bathroom?"

00:06:12.037 --> 00:06:13.372
-And I remember at the time
going like,

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:15.274
"Nobody has a flashlight."

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:18.677
-So she roots through.
She said, "Dinner roll,

00:06:18.677 --> 00:06:22.715
lip balm, wrench. Wait.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.983
Oh, I found a pad of butter."
I'm not kidding you.

00:06:24.983 --> 00:06:26.885
This is what she has
in her purse.

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:28.654
And then she locates
a flashlight.

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:31.490
She says, "We're in luck."
So it's a little pen thing.

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:35.494
So the two of them take off
and very slow progress.

00:06:35.494 --> 00:06:36.996
-Yeah.
-And all of a sudden --

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:38.831
-Slow and loud.
-Yeah.

00:06:38.831 --> 00:06:40.633
Crazy loud. Jingle jangle.
-Yeah.

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:45.103
-So all of a sudden, a door --
The theater is flooded in light.

00:06:45.103 --> 00:06:47.005
They've opened the door
to the outside.

00:06:47.005 --> 00:06:48.541
They thought it
was the bathroom.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:49.775
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:51.376
The sun's pouring in.

00:06:51.376 --> 00:06:55.147
-Yeah, just these
two nutty aunts

00:06:55.147 --> 00:06:57.817
silhouetted by the daytime sun

00:06:57.817 --> 00:07:00.953
as they go out on the fire
escape looking for the bathroom.

00:07:00.953 --> 00:07:03.856
-And this one --
This one grabs my hand and says,

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:06.926
"For the love of God, Mother,
do something."

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:09.762
[ Laughter ]
I said, "What? What can I do?"

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:12.131
-So I had to run over
and grab -- wrangle

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:13.900
my aunts back to their seats.
-Yeah.

00:07:13.900 --> 00:07:16.335
-But it was a lovely story.

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:18.604
It was one
that was often retold.

00:07:18.604 --> 00:07:22.208
And I am very thankful for
all our time with Sherry.

00:07:22.208 --> 00:07:23.676
-Exactly.
-She will be missed.

00:07:23.676 --> 00:07:26.011
-Rest in peace.
-Rest in peace.

00:07:26.011 --> 00:07:28.714
So here we are.
Dad, are you good?

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.549
Are you excited
that you're testing negative

00:07:30.549 --> 00:07:32.684
and you're going
to be able to see us?

00:07:32.684 --> 00:07:34.386
-Yeah. Really excited.

00:07:34.386 --> 00:07:36.155
Really looking forward to it.

00:07:36.155 --> 00:07:38.691
-Alright, good.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:40.859
-I just have to leave Albert.
That's the downside.

00:07:40.859 --> 00:07:44.263
-Yeah. Well, you guys, thank you
for being with us.

00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:45.731
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

